    love: "Third-decan Leos tend to be passionate, protective partners. They often pursue love with energy and enjoy a relationship with spark, including a little friendly competition. They are fiercely loyal and may become defensive if a loved one is threatened. Patience in disagreements can be harder for them. A partner who meets their strength with confidence, respects their independence and is not intimidated by their intensity tends to suit them well. Learning to soften in conflict and listen fully deepens intimacy for this decan.",
    work: "At work, this decan often thrives in competitive, fast-paced or high-stakes environments. Sports, the military, emergency services, entrepreneurship, sales, law and leadership roles that require courage can suit them. They are decisive and often willing to take risks others avoid. Slow consensus-building may frustrate them. Their growth area is collaboration: involving others in decisions rather than leading alone. When they combine their drive with patience, they can become exceptionally effective leaders who inspire loyalty as well as respect. Clear targets and a scoreboard of some kind tend to bring out their best effort.",
    growth: "For third-decan Leos, growth often lies in channelling energy wisely. Regular physical activity can help release tension and keep moods steady. Try pausing before reacting in conflict, giving others space to finish speaking. Notice when competitiveness helps and when it harms relationships. Celebrating teamwork as much as personal victory can broaden their influence. Their courage is a genuine gift, and it shines brightest when tempered with patience, humility and an awareness that strength can also mean restraint. Martial arts, rowing or team sport can turn the same fire into discipline rather than friction.",
