    love: "Third-decan Virgos are often the most romantic members of their sign, though their romance is understated. They court with handwritten notes, carefully chosen gifts and evenings planned down to the playlist. Tenderness comes more easily than for many Virgos, and so does a wish for a calm, pleasant home life. Insecurity can surface as self-criticism, especially about whether they are attractive or interesting enough. A partner who offers sincere, specific compliments and reciprocates their thoughtfulness usually finds a devoted, gentle companion who keeps improving the shared life in small, lovely ways.",
    work: "Work that marries precision with taste tends to suit this decan best. Interior and graphic design, tailoring, horticulture, copy-editing, patisserie, beauty therapy, curation and patient-facing care all draw on the blend of Venus and Virgo. They are often the person who makes a report readable, a shop window inviting or a clinic waiting room less bleak. Colleagues appreciate their tact. What they sometimes neglect is self-advocacy: their contributions are so smoothly delivered that others underestimate the effort. Keeping a record of results and naming them at review time helps.",
